# DWT working practices

Live repo, only one designer committing at the moment, grown organically:

- Read the neighbouring pages/folders before creating or editing anything, and match their pattern even where it's not the textbook Prototype Kit way.
- Don't restructure. Never rename, move, or delete existing folders, pages, or routes as a side effect of another task — flag it and ask first.
- Prefer additive changes — new pages and versions alongside what's there. Don't edit earlier versions in place, unless explicitly asked to fix an existing page. `v1` and `v2` are the research versions.
- Work in the latest version (currently `v4`) unless told otherwise. Its layout (`layouts/v4.html`), views and `registerV4Routes()` are the ones to edit.
- Match the surrounding file's casing, spacing, and comment style rather than "correcting" it repo-wide.
- Keep scope tight — touch only the files the task needs.
- When a change affects a version's behaviour, update its `versions/vN.html` page (changes table and reason) and the date on the index card.
- When a version or Jira design reference page adds or changes a screen, add or update its variant in `app/data/design-index.js` (shown at `/design`), newest first, with a sentence on what made it different. The Design page only links out — never add screens to it.

## Git

- Commit and push straight to `main`. There is currently one designer working on this repo, so no feature branch or pull request is needed. Still check `git status`/`git branch` first, and only commit the files the task touched. If other designers start committing again, revisit this rule.
- Commit messages: short, plain-English, sentence case (e.g. "Add Create/rotate/delete API key journey to software provider detail") — not Conventional Commits.
- `routes.js` and `app/views/index.html` are shared, high-traffic files — keep diffs minimal and additive there.
